			"notes": "## e4BTA 0.2.0\n\nInitial public release of e4BTA for Better Than Adventure 8.0.1.\n\ne4BTA tunnels BTA multiplayer connections through Steam Networking Messages using Spacewar (App ID 480), allowing players to host and join without router port forwarding.\n\n### Requirements\n\n- Better Than Adventure 8.0.1\n- Fabric Loader 0.18.4-bta.11 or newer compatible Babric version\n- Java 17 or newer\n- Steam running and signed in\n- The same e4BTA JAR installed on the server and every joining client\n\n### Installation\n\n1. Place the JAR in the dedicated server's `mods` folder.\n2. Place the same JAR in every player's client `mods` folder.\n3. Start Steam and sign in.\n4. Start the server normally.\n5. Wait for `Steam tunnel ready` in the server log.\n6. Share the displayed Steam server address with your Steam friends.\n\nNo port forwarding is required.\n\n### Notes\n\n- This release is specifically for BTA 8.0.1.\n- Modern Minecraft e4steam clients are not compatible with e4BTA servers.\n- The server must run through a normal signed-in Steam desktop session.\n- This is the first public release, so please report reproducible problems through GitHub Issues.\n\n### Credits\n\ne4BTA is maintained by Verse and is based on Kamilchik's e4steam project, which is derived from e4mc by Skye and contributors.\n\nSee the repository's `LICENSE`, `NOTICE`, and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` files for complete licensing and attribution information.\n\n### SHA-256\n\n`167FBAA7B034088EBC7CFBD7E8B8283BE5AA8699D689411C95E811E501670598`"
